# Tooling

Python 3.12. Stack: uv, FastAPI, uvicorn, SQLModel, Typer, Rich, pytest, ruff, SQLite.

## uv only

Every Python, install, and test command goes through `uv`. Never `pip`, never bare `python` / `pytest` / `ruff`.

```bash
# ❌ BAD
pip install fastapi
python -m pytest
ruff check .

# ✅ GOOD
uv add fastapi
uv add --dev pytest ruff
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check
uv run uvicorn atlas.api.app:app --reload
```

Use `uv add` / `uv add --dev` / `uv sync`. The lockfile is `uv.lock`; do not invent a `requirements.txt`.

## Pre-commit gates

Before every commit, both must pass:

1. `uv run ruff check`
2. `uv run pytest`

Fix failures in the same cycle. Do not commit with failing lint or tests.

## One todo, one commit

Each assigned plan todo is one cycle: implement, lint, test, update `docs/architecture.md`, then a single focused commit. Stop after that commit so the change can be reviewed before the next todo starts. Do not batch multiple todos into one commit.
